+
+// The share of draws, 0 to 1, on which a pixel whose history of a kind holds `historyLength` draws traces a ray of its
+// own to catch up. 1 is today's rate under FullRateFrames. `cap` is the history's cap at the pixel, in draws. `young`
+// says that the history restarted less than the shape's end ago (youngHistory). A history that is not young keeps
+// today's rule, an own ray in every draw while it is under FullRateFrames: the anti-lag holds about 17 % of a settled
+// view's diffuse histories between 8 and 32 draws for good (t0-gumm's record), and the length alone cannot tell them
+// from a history that grows after a restart, so a share of the length past FullRateFrames would trace own rays there
+// for ever. A pixel whose cap is under FullRateFrames also keeps today's rule. So a settled history traces exactly
+// today's own rays, and the share ends at the cap at the latest.
+float catchUpShare(float historyLength, float cap, bool young)
+{
+    if (!young || cap < FullRateFrames)
+        return historyLength < FullRateFrames ? 1.0 : 0.0;
+    float end = min(trace.catchUpEnd, cap);
+    if (historyLength >= end)
+        return 0.0;
+    return trace.catchUpPeak * (trace.catchUpFall == 0.0 ? 1.0 : pow(1.0 - historyLength / end, trace.catchUpFall));
