+// Whether the pixel takes its turn of the catch-up rays of the kind in this draw, for a share of 0 to 1. A share of 1
+// is always true and a share of 0 never. The phase steps by 2^32 / the golden ratio per draw, so a pixel's turns come at
+// nearly even gaps of 1 / share draws; its offset is the blue-noise mask's first frame at the pixel (red for the
+// reflections, green for the diffuse rays) in its high 8 bits and a hash of the pixel in the low 24, so the pixels that
+// take their turn in one draw are spread evenly with no clumps, and small shares still get distinct offsets.
+bool catchUpTurn(ivec2 pixel, uint kind, float share)
+{
